From 250ef65851efd4705a31af1eef7698f50f0a97be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:00:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hir_typeck: an ivar set to an opaque projection keeps it opaque

HMTypeInferrence::set_ivar_to erases lifetimes by re-monomorphising the
type with an identity Monomorphiser, and Monomorphiser::monomorph_type
clears the binding of an Opaque path, since a real substitution can change
what it names. So an ivar set to `<Self as Hash>::Engine/*O*/` held it as
an unbound projection, and a method call on a local of that type paused
("Unbound type path, pausing") until compact_ivars re-expanded it at the
end of a pass. When nothing else changed in that pass, typeck stabilised
with the call still pending. bitcoin_hashes 0.12.0 lib.rs:193 (dtool
0.17.0), a provided method with `type Engine: HashEngine`:

    fn hash(data: &[u8]) -> Self {
        let mut engine = Self::engine();
        engine.input(data);
        Self::from_engine(engine)
    }

    lib.rs:193:28 warn:0: Spare rule - _CallMethod {<Self as Hash>::Engine}.input({&[u8]}, ) -> _/*6*/
    BUG: src/hir_typeck/expr_cs.cpp:8543: Spare rules left after typecheck stabilised

The lifetime-erasing monomorphiser now keeps an Opaque binding (generics map
to themselves there). The same call as the block's last statement worked
only because the `()` fallback forced another pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp b/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp
index 29358661..c2ff4aa7 100644
--- a/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp
+++ b/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp
@@ -877,6 +877,17 @@ void HMTypeInferrence::set_ivar_to(unsigned int slot, ::HIR::TypeRef type)
                 }
                 return HIR::LifetimeRef();
             }
+            // Generics map to themselves, so an opaque projection is still opaque (the default clears the binding,
+            // as a substitution can change what it names). Stored unbound, a method call on it waited for a re-expansion,
+            // which only came with another pass: `let mut engine = Self::engine(); engine.input(data); ..` in a
+            // provided method, `type Engine: HashEngine` - bitcoin_hashes 0.12.0 lib.rs:193, "Spare rule - _CallMethod".
+            ::HIR::TypeRef monomorph_type(const Span& sp, const ::HIR::TypeRef& tpl, bool allow_infer) const override {
+                auto rv = Monomorphiser::monomorph_type(sp, tpl, allow_infer);
+                if( tpl.data().is_Path() && tpl.data().as_Path().binding.is_Opaque() ) {
+                    rv.get_unique().as_Path().binding = tpl.data().as_Path().binding.clone();
+                }
+                return rv;
+            }
 
             Monomorph_AddLifetimes() {}
         };
